194763e4d0","position":"1786619869982874001-71104e0c-c75e-4c75-ab46-ba63441c53ad"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c24dbd12f9621b90ca3e300b158d2aa4ac3efab82653bbc1517c923bb93da15d","event_uuid":"226f3602-9fc9-43f9-b068-82e45a12bdd3","position":{"commit_sha":"0fe5dacbdd4ff3c72ce820ab2c069a628c2191b1","position":"1786619874600742001-226f3602-9fc9-43f9-b068-82e45a12bdd3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 1723 (a1cea85118). Premise re-verification against HEAD 641ba8bed1 — all four claimed defects were still present: (1) bare --assignee handles at README.md:44+50 and docs/user-guide.md:115,234; (2) docs/README.md:25 routing MCP to llm-framework.md; (3) docs/README.md:91 describing config.md via the removed .rebar/config.conf reader; (4) pyproject.toml:490 calling non-core mypy advisory-only while Makefile:248 and _build-and-test.yml gate it over the whole library. No sibling had fixed any of them. One extra site beyond the original plan was found and fixed: README.md:50's library block taught the same bare handle via assignee=\"alice\". Local gates: ten check_* gates OK, complexity baseline clean, four generators produce no diff, make lint + make typecheck green, full CI test selection 12724 passed (the 4 errors were self-inflicted — I committed while the run was in flight, tripping the HEAD-guard fixture — and the 1 failure was the known order-dependent decline flake; all 5 pass serially at stable HEAD).","timestamp":1786617681517535001}],"created_at":1786212630660603001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6568389b-2bfd-469a-aeb5-fb3b08e1ac57","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ae1b-b2a0-a080-4b4e"},{"link_uuid":"cf77aa64-05dc-4d0f-93f1-407dbd3c25c1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4497-9222-63a2-4f59"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFour authoritative-looking doc/comment entry points have drifted from current contracts (audit ae1b). Premises RE-VERIFIED against HEAD 641ba8bed1 — all four still present:\n- **Bare `--assignee <handle>` teaches a Jira-UNRESOLVABLE value.** `README.md:44` (`rebar claim \"$tid\" --assignee alice`) and `README.md:50` (the adjacent library block, `rebar.claim(tid, assignee=\"alice\")`), `docs/user-guide.md:115` (`rebar claim <ticket-id> --assignee alice`), `docs/user-guide.md:234` (`rebar edit <id> --priority=1 --assignee=bob --add-tag=urgent`). Yet `docs/config.md:461-467` documents `ticket.default_assignee` and requires a Jira-resolvable identity — a bare handle is silently cleared by the next reconcile.\n- **MCP navigation mis-route**: `docs/README.md:25` routes \"Drive rebar over MCP\" → `llm-framework.md`, while the complete generated tool reference is `docs/mcp-reference.md` (itself indexed at `docs/README.md:77`).\n- **Removed config surface**: `docs/README.md:91` still describes `config.md` as covering the flat `.rebar/config.conf` keys; `docs/config.md:13,519` already record that reader as REMOVED in favour of `rebar.toml` / a `[tool.rebar]` pyproject table.\n- **Stale mypy comment**: `pyproject.toml:488-490` says the non-core tree \"is checked advisory-only for now,\" but CI GATES mypy over the whole library (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` \"GATING: mypy over the WHOLE library AND scripts/\", and `Makefile:248` `typecheck: ## ... mypy over the whole library + scripts/ (gating)`).\n\n## Approach\nCorrect each drifted example/label/comment against the CURRENT contract; no behavior change.\n- In the two quickstart claim examples (`README.md:44`, `docs/user-guide.md:115`) **omit `--assignee` entirely** — `claim` then applies the configured `ticket.default_assignee` (`docs/config.md:466`), which is the behaviour AGENTS.md tells agents to use. Same for the adjacent library line `README.md:50` → `rebar.claim(tid)`. Adjust the trailing alignment comment on `README.md:44` so the fence stays tidy.\n- Where an assignee value is genuinely illustrative (`docs/user-guide.md:234`, the `rebar edit` field example) substitute an email form (`--assignee=alice@example.com`) that IS Jira-resolvable, and add a one-clause note in the surrounding prose pointing at `config.md`'s Jira-resolvable requirement.\n- `docs/README.md:25` → link `mcp-reference.md` (keeping `llm-framework.md` mentioned for the agent/gate operations, so no index entry is orphaned).\n- `docs/README.md:91` → describe `config.md` as `rebar.toml` / `[tool.rebar]` keys, precedence, and design of record.\n- `pyproject.toml:488-490` → state that mypy is gated over the whole library and `scripts/`, with `[[tool.mypy.overrides]]` layering the extra `disallow_untyped_defs` ratchet on the promoted packages.\n\n## Scope (docs + one TOML comment only)\n- `README.md` — quickstart claim example (44) and the adjacent library example (50).\n- `docs/user-guide.md` — claim example (115) and `edit` example (234) + one clause of surrounding prose.\n- `docs/README.md` — MCP route (25) and the `config.md` description (91).\n- `pyproject.toml` — the `[tool.mypy]` header comment (488-490). No `[tool.mypy]` VALUES change; the ratchet-flip is explicitly out of scope (pyproject.toml is contended, per the epic).\n- NOT changed: `docs/identity.md:184` (legitimately cites legacy `.rebar/config.conf` as a per-machine override), `docs/release-notes.md:361` (historical removal record), `docs/cli-reference.md` (GENERATED from CLI help — its `--assignee` strings are option syntax, not a value example), `docs/exit-codes.md:78` / `README.md:345` (`<you>` placeholders, not bare handles).\n\n## Risk / generator + gate interactions\n- None of the four edited files are generator-owned (the generators are `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`, `gen_mcp_reference.py`, `gen_env_registry.py`, `gen_adr_index.py`, targeting `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`, `docs/env-vars.md`, the ADR index — none in scope).\n- `scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py` EXTRACTS and EXECUTES the README `## Quickstart` bash block in CI; `tests/scripts/test_check_readme_quickstart.py::test_extract_real_readme_has_golden_path_commands` asserts it still contains `rebar init` / `rebar create` / `rebar claim` / `rebar transition`. Dropping only the `--assignee alice` argument keeps all four needles and keeps the block runnable (`claim` without `--assignee` is the documented default path), so both stay green. That test's other `--assignee alice` occurrences are its OWN synthetic fixtures and are not touched.\n- `scripts/check_docs_index.py` checks docs-index completeness and dead links: changing `docs/README.md:25`'s target from `llm-framework.md` to `mcp-reference.md` keeps both files indexed elsewhere (`llm-framework.md` and `mcp-reference.md` each retain their own index entries), so no file becomes unindexed and no link becomes dead.\n\n## Verification\n- Docs/comment-only: no `src/rebar/**` and no test-behavior changes; the existing docs/link/golden gates stay green.\n- Full local gate set before push: the ten `scripts/check_*` gates, generator no-diff vs `git archive HEAD`, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the CI test selection `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"`.\n- Each corrected truth is confirmed by a grep assertion below rather than by manual reading.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No quickstart/user-guide example teaches a Jira-unresolvable bare handle: `grep -rnE '\\-\\-assignee[= ]+[A-Za-z]+([^@A-Za-z]|$)' README.md docs/user-guide.md` returns nothing, and `grep -n 'assignee=\"alice\"' README.md` returns nothing.\n- [x] `grep -n 'Drive rebar over MCP' -A1 docs/README.md` links `mcp-reference.md`, and `grep -n 'config\\.conf' docs/README.md` returns nothing.\n- [x] `grep -n 'advisory-only for now' pyproject.toml` returns nothing and the `[tool.mypy]` header comment names whole-library (+`scripts/`) gating; `git diff pyproject.toml` shows comment lines only (no key/value change).\n- [x] `git diff --name-only origin/main` lists exactly `README.md`, `docs/README.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `pyproject.toml` — no `src/rebar/**`, no `tests/**`.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py`, `python scripts/check_docs_index.py`, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"` all pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"README.md","reason":"Fix bare --assignee alice example (line 44)"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"Fix --assignee examples (lines 115, 229)"},{"path":"docs/README.md","reason":"Fix MCP route (25) and config.conf description (91)"},{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"Update stale mypy advisory-only comment to whole-library gating"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07"],["relates_to","4497-9222-63a2-4f59"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07","parent_status_uuid":"71104e0c-c75e-4c75-ab46-ba63441c53ad","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["documentation","docs-drift","audit-follow-up"],"ticket_id":"879f-5549-91e3-4d6f","ticket_type":"task","title":"Correct user-facing configuration, assignee, MCP, and optionality documentation drift","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e8412f33-28b8-463f-834d-09c16d10aa87","14c0a3e2-885c-4dc5-996e-d2e1993419f4","6568389b-2bfd-469a-aeb5-fb3b08e1ac57","fd1f66dc-c07a-4f18-b391-e10af818751d","ed27256a-bbde-485b-9409-e43a2958c6fd","de68ea76-a65d-46a0-b6f6-0f691123c0ef","7fbccd4d-bf77-4b92-8d3b-8d13a1369e33","4c97dcaa-2817-4485-b8ac-5746198ad506","16ff7b24-0001-45b6-a369-99734a4ba15e","90b74c5e-87dc-4f53-bc96-9adda604a69a","c7019733-1ea0-4fba-af18-7a32b42c3959","8c88a1a7-02d8-412c-9e17-ff0e32591c3f","7fa7f0ce-da2b-44c4-95cf-6ea630b855cc","cf77aa64-05dc-4d0f-93f1-407dbd3c25c1","13a2b61c-5350-4d4d-9bb8-0698c7542778","71104e0c-c75e-4c75-ab46-ba63441c53ad","226f3602-9fc9-43f9-b068-82e45a12bdd3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659630404338001,"uuid":"9adef7bc-d64d-4878-bf5c-dd2e66ea0430"}